WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.810
All right, guys, I am now ready to say.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:08.650
On the heels of the confirmation of Donald
Trump's nominee to the Supreme Court, Amy

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:16.339
CONI Barrett, that Joe Biden and Democrats,
if given the opportunity, must expand the

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:17.869
Supreme Court.

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:23.439
Of course, this depends on taking the White
House, taking the Senate, keeping control

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:24.970
of the House of Representatives.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:29.550
I'm going to be calling it expanding the court
rather than packing the court.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.489
When you say packing the court, you're already
ceding some ground to the right and making

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:39.329
it sound like something outrageous or radical
or aggressive when it's not.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:46.280
I've made it very clear that on moral questions,
the left must not stoop down to where the

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:52.790
right is when it comes to dishonesty and authoritarianism
and the perversion of justice.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:59.839
But when it comes to using the systems, we
have to legally fight against double standards

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:02.670
and hypocrisy and absurdity.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.640
We actually have a responsibility to do it.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.040
So let's go through and talk about it piece
by piece.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:16.360
There are some on the right who say adding
justices to the Supreme Court would be a crazy,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:22.380
unprecedented, authoritarian, undemocratic
thing for a hypothetical President Joe Biden

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.560
to do.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.850
This is completely untrue.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.759
John Adams reduced the size of the court from
six to five.

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:34.630
Thomas Jefferson went back from five to six
and subsequently up to seven under Andrew

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:35.630
Jackson.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.000
The court went from seven to nine justices.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.210
So the idea that it's not something that has
been done is wrong.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:47.630
Now, there are some even on the left who oppose
expanding the Supreme Court because of the

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:54.990
slippery slope possibility that if Joe Biden
expands the court, the next Republican, faced

00:01:54.990 --> 00:02:01.710
with a minority on their side on the court,
will then expand the court again.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:06.010
And then the next Democratic spans the court
again and on and on and on.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:11.000
First of all, this is silly at its face because
at a certain point, how big is the court going

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
to get?

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.010
Ninety seven justices, 131 justices.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:16.380
It's not going to happen.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.650
Okay, because the public wouldn't actually
stand for it.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.340
And I'm going to get back to that momentarily.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.790
But importantly, expanding the court is not
actually that easy.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.319
If you have the same party controlling the
White House, the Senate and the House, which

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:39.290
we could have from 2021 to 2023, if Democrats
take the White House and the Senate, expanding

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.750
the court is not that different from passing
an appropriations bill.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.650
But there are two reasons why it's unlikely
that we would go in this slippery slope direction

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.550
of indefinite expansion of the Supreme Court.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:57.760
And the first is it's not actually that common
that the same party controls the White House,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:04.450
the House and the Senate at a time when the
public would be okay with an expansion of

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.450
the court.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:10.920
Barack Obama had the White House, House and
Senate for two out of his eight years.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:17.880
And it's very common that at least one of
those three is controlled by an opposing party.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:23.470
But maybe more importantly, there are many
political circumstances that don't lend themselves

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.300
to public approval of expanding the court.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:31.879
And if the circumstances don't lend themselves
to expanding the court and a Republican or

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:38.730
Democratic controlled House, Senate and White
House decides to do it when the public isn't

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:44.200
in the mode that they believe it is appropriate,
they will be punished electorally if Donald

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:50.519
Trump is defeated and Democrats take the Senate
and we retain control of the House.

00:03:50.519 --> 00:03:56.090
It will be one of those times where the public
will be okay with expanding the court because

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.010
the public knows the absurdity of the last
four years.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.300
The public knows the ridiculous double standard
of Republicans saying no Merrick Garland during

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.360
the last year of Barack Obama's term.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:14.090
But yes, Amy CONI Barrett, in the last week
of Donald Trump's term, the urgent need to

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:21.490
right that wrong, I believe, will give us
a population from 2021 to 2023.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.400
That would be okay with an expansion of the
court if indeed Democrats take the Senate

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.400
and the White House.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.680
So not only is there nothing unconstitutional
about expanding the court, not only is there

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:38.030
nothing unprecedented about expanding the
court, not only is there nothing set in stone

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:43.480
that one expansion will inevitably lead to
every future president expanding the court.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.770
But if Joe Biden wins the White House and
Democrats take the Senate, we will have a

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:54.070
unique two year period during which the country
will understand that to get back on a more

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:59.140
correct path, we must take less common action.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:04.420
And one of those actions is expanding the
court to get it back from these outrageous

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.500
lunatics that Donald Trump has put on the
court.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:13.450
And for those saying that while it may not
be unconstitutional and it may not be undemocratic,

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:17.350
the reality is it is actually democratic.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.350
Republicans have nominated.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.251
Well, I'm sorry I said that wrong for those
saying it might not be unconstitutional, but

00:05:23.251 --> 00:05:25.440
it is undemocratic.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.740
Understand that Republicans have nominated
15 of the last 19 justices despite having

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:35.010
lost the popular vote in six of the last seven
presidential elections.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:39.060
That doesn't sound democratic to me if you
disagree with me.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.060
Let me know.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:06:24.550
I want to hear 

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:46.740
from you.

